{
  "title": "Stage 3: Events",
  "summary": "Raise an OrderProcessed event and let a printer, a totals board and an audit log subscribe and unsubscribe.",
  "minutes": 25,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Who wants to know?",
      "body": [
        "More people care about each order now. The console wants a line, the managers want a totals board, compliance wants an audit log. If the loop calls each of them, the loop has to know every one, and adding a fourth listener means editing it again.",
        "",
        "Turn it around: the code that processes an order just **announces** the outcome, and anyone interested subscribes.",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "class OrderDesk",
        "{",
        "    public event Action<Outcome>? OrderProcessed;",
        "",
        "    public void Process(Order order)",
        "    {",
        "        // validate, store ...",
        "        OrderProcessed?.Invoke(outcome);   // tell every subscriber",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "desk.OrderProcessed += outcome => Console.WriteLine(Format(outcome));",
        "desk.OrderProcessed += board.Record;     // a method group works too",
        "```",
        "",
        "- An `event` holds a list of methods. `+=` subscribes, `-=` unsubscribes, and only `OrderDesk` can raise it.",
        "- `?.Invoke` raises it safely: with no subscribers the event is `null`, and nothing happens.",
        "- Subscribers run in the order they subscribed, one after another. That is why the console line for an order is always printed before the next order is processed.",
        "",
        "`Action<Outcome>` is fine here; `EventHandler<T>` is the convention for public libraries. The outcome is a record with an enum:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "enum Status { Accepted, Rejected }",
        "",
        "record Outcome(Order Order, Status Status, string Reason);",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var bell = new Bell();",
        "Action<string> shout = name => Console.WriteLine($\"{name}!\");",
        "",
        "bell.Rang += name => Console.WriteLine($\"hello {name}\");",
        "bell.Rang += shout;",
        "bell.Ring(\"ann\");",
        "",
        "bell.Rang -= shout;",
        "bell.Ring(\"bo\");",
        "",
        "class Bell",
        "{",
        "    public event Action<string>? Rang;",
        "    public void Ring(string name) => Rang?.Invoke(name);",
        "}"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "hello ann",
        "ann!",
        "hello bo"
      ],
      "explain": "Both subscribers run, in subscription order. `-= shout` works because `shout` is the same delegate that was added. You could not remove the first lambda: there is no variable holding it."
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Arrange `Process` so that the order is validated, then stored, and only then announced.",
      "lines": [
        "    public void Process(Order order)",
        "    {",
        "        var result = Validate(order);",
        "        if (result.IsOk)",
        "            result = _orders.Add(order);",
        "        var outcome = result.IsOk",
        "            ? new Outcome(order, Status.Accepted, \"\")",
        "            : new Outcome(order, Status.Rejected, result.Error);",
        "        OrderProcessed?.Invoke(outcome);",
        "    }"
      ],
      "explain": "Subscribers must hear the final verdict, which includes the duplicate check in `Add`. Raising the event before storing would announce `accepted` for an order the store then refuses."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Which line can code **outside** `OrderDesk` legally write?",
      "options": [
        "`desk.OrderProcessed += audit.Record;`",
        "`desk.OrderProcessed?.Invoke(fakeOutcome);`",
        "`desk.OrderProcessed = null;`",
        "`var count = desk.OrderProcessed.GetInvocationList().Length;`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "From outside, an event allows only `+=` and `-=`. Raising it, clearing it or inspecting its list are reserved for the class that owns it. That is the whole point of the `event` keyword over a public delegate field."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Announce every outcome",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Move the processing into a class and let subscribers do the reporting.",
        "",
        "1. Add `enum Status { Accepted, Rejected }` and `record Outcome(Order Order, Status Status, string Reason)` (the reason is `\"\"` when accepted).",
        "2. Write `class OrderDesk` with a constructor taking the `List<IOrderRule>` and the `IRepository<Order>`, a `public event Action<Outcome>? OrderProcessed`, and `void Process(Order order)` that validates, stores and raises the event. Move `Validate` into it.",
        "3. Write `class TotalsBoard` with `Accepted` and `Rejected` counts, units accepted per product, and a `void Record(Outcome outcome)` method.",
        "4. In the program, subscribe a lambda that prints the outcome line, and subscribe `board.Record`. The loop just calls `desk.Process(order)`.",
        "",
        "The summary now comes from the board, and gains a units line: `Units: ` then each product with accepted units, in enum order (`Widget`, `Gadget`, `Gizmo`), as `NAME COUNT` joined by `, `, or `Units: none`. The `Unreadable` count stays in the main program.",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "1,alice,widget,3",
        "2,bob,gadget,2",
        "3,carol,widget,4",
        "4,dave,gizmo,1",
        "5,erin,gadget,1",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
        "#2 bob Gadget x2 accepted",
        "#3 carol Widget x4 accepted",
        "#4 dave Gizmo x1 rejected: Gizmo is discontinued",
        "#5 erin Gadget x1 accepted",
        "Accepted: 4, Rejected: 1, Unreadable: 0",
        "Units: Widget 7, Gadget 3",
        "Stored: #1, #2, #3, #5",
        "```",
        "",
        "Every earlier line must still print exactly as before."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var rules = new List<IOrderRule>",
        "{",
        "    new MinQuantityRule(),",
        "    new MaxQuantityRule(10),",
        "    new DiscontinuedRule(Product.Gizmo),",
        "    new BlockedCustomerRule(\"mallory\"),",
        "};",
        "",
        "IRepository<Order> orders = new SortedRepository<Order>();",
        "",
        "int accepted = 0, rejected = 0, unreadable = 0;",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "",
        "    var order = ParseOrder(line);",
        "    if (order is null)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"line {lineNumber}: cannot read '{line}'\");",
        "        unreadable++;",
        "        continue;",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    var result = Validate(order);",
        "    if (result.IsOk)",
        "        result = orders.Add(order);",
        "",
        "    if (result.IsOk)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{Describe(order)} accepted\");",
        "        accepted++;",
        "    }",
        "    else",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{Describe(order)} rejected: {result.Error}\");",
        "        rejected++;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Accepted: {accepted}, Rejected: {rejected}, Unreadable: {unreadable}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine(StoredLine(orders.All()));",
        "",
        "Result<Order> Validate(Order order)",
        "{",
        "    var reasons = rules.Select(rule => rule.Check(order)).OfType<string>().ToList();",
        "    return reasons.Count == 0",
        "        ? Result<Order>.Ok(order)",
        "        : Result<Order>.Fail(string.Join(\"; \", reasons));",
        "}",
        "",
        "string StoredLine(IReadOnlyList<Order> stored) =>",
        "    stored.Count == 0",
        "        ? \"Stored: none\"",
        "        : \"Stored: \" + string.Join(\", \", stored.Select(o => $\"#{o.Id}\"));",
        "",
        "Order? ParseOrder(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[0], out var id)) return null;",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Product>(parts[2], ignoreCase: true, out var product) || !Enum.IsDefined(product)) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out var quantity)) return null;",
        "    return new Order(id, parts[1], product, quantity);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Describe(Order order) => $\"#{order.Id} {order.Customer} {order.Product} x{order.Quantity}\";",
        "",
        "enum Product { Widget, Gadget, Gizmo }",
        "",
        "record Order(int Id, string Customer, Product Product, int Quantity) : IEntity;",
        "",
        "interface IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    string? Check(Order order);",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MinQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity < 1 ? \"quantity must be at least 1\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MaxQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly int _max;",
        "",
        "    public MaxQuantityRule(int max) => _max = max;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity > _max ? $\"quantity over {_max}\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class DiscontinuedRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly Product _product;",
        "",
        "    public DiscontinuedRule(Product product) => _product = product;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Product == _product ? $\"{_product} is discontinued\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class BlockedCustomerRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly string _customer;",
        "",
        "    public BlockedCustomerRule(string customer) => _customer = customer;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Customer == _customer ? $\"customer {_customer} is blocked\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "interface IEntity",
        "{",
        "    int Id { get; }",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Result<T>(bool IsOk, T? Value, string Error)",
        "{",
        "    public static Result<T> Ok(T value) => new(true, value, \"\");",
        "    public static Result<T> Fail(string error) => new(false, default, error);",
        "}",
        "",
        "interface IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    Result<T> Add(T item);",
        "    T? Find(int id);",
        "    IReadOnlyList<T> All();",
        "}",
        "",
        "class ListRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    private readonly List<T> _items = new();",
        "",
        "    public Result<T> Add(T item)",
        "    {",
        "        if (Find(item.Id) is not null)",
        "            return Result<T>.Fail($\"duplicate id {item.Id}\");",
        "        _items.Add(item);",
        "        return Result<T>.Ok(item);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public T? Find(int id) => _items.FirstOrDefault(i => i.Id == id);",
        "",
        "    public IReadOnlyList<T> All() => _items;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class SortedRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    private readonly SortedDictionary<int, T> _items = new();",
        "",
        "    public Result<T> Add(T item)",
        "    {",
        "        if (!_items.TryAdd(item.Id, item))",
        "            return Result<T>.Fail($\"duplicate id {item.Id}\");",
        "        return Result<T>.Ok(item);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public T? Find(int id) => _items.TryGetValue(id, out var item) ? item : default;",
        "",
        "    public IReadOnlyList<T> All() => _items.Values.ToList();",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "var rules = new List<IOrderRule>",
        "{",
        "    new MinQuantityRule(),",
        "    new MaxQuantityRule(10),",
        "    new DiscontinuedRule(Product.Gizmo),",
        "    new BlockedCustomerRule(\"mallory\"),",
        "};",
        "",
        "IRepository<Order> orders = new SortedRepository<Order>();",
        "var desk = new OrderDesk(rules, orders);",
        "var board = new TotalsBoard();",
        "",
        "desk.OrderProcessed += outcome => Console.WriteLine(Format(outcome));",
        "desk.OrderProcessed += board.Record;",
        "",
        "var unreadable = 0;",
        "var lineNumber = 0;",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    lineNumber++;",
        "    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;",
        "    var order = ParseOrder(line);",
        "    if (order is null)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"line {lineNumber}: cannot read '{line}'\");",
        "        unreadable++;",
        "        continue;",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    desk.Process(order);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Accepted: {board.Accepted}, Rejected: {board.Rejected}, Unreadable: {unreadable}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine(board.UnitsLine());",
        "Console.WriteLine(StoredLine(orders.All()));",
        "string Format(Outcome outcome) =>",
        "    outcome.Status == Status.Accepted",
        "        ? $\"{Describe(outcome.Order)} accepted\"",
        "        : $\"{Describe(outcome.Order)} rejected: {outcome.Reason}\";",
        "",
        "string StoredLine(IReadOnlyList<Order> stored) =>",
        "    stored.Count == 0",
        "        ? \"Stored: none\"",
        "        : \"Stored: \" + string.Join(\", \", stored.Select(o => $\"#{o.Id}\"));",
        "",
        "Order? ParseOrder(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',', StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);",
        "    if (parts.Length != 4) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[0], out var id)) return null;",
        "    if (!Enum.TryParse<Product>(parts[2], ignoreCase: true, out var product) || !Enum.IsDefined(product)) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out var quantity)) return null;",
        "    return new Order(id, parts[1], product, quantity);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Describe(Order order) => $\"#{order.Id} {order.Customer} {order.Product} x{order.Quantity}\";",
        "",
        "enum Product { Widget, Gadget, Gizmo }",
        "",
        "record Order(int Id, string Customer, Product Product, int Quantity) : IEntity;",
        "",
        "interface IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    string? Check(Order order);",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MinQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity < 1 ? \"quantity must be at least 1\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class MaxQuantityRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly int _max;",
        "",
        "    public MaxQuantityRule(int max) => _max = max;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Quantity > _max ? $\"quantity over {_max}\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class DiscontinuedRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly Product _product;",
        "",
        "    public DiscontinuedRule(Product product) => _product = product;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Product == _product ? $\"{_product} is discontinued\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class BlockedCustomerRule : IOrderRule",
        "{",
        "    private readonly string _customer;",
        "",
        "    public BlockedCustomerRule(string customer) => _customer = customer;",
        "",
        "    public string? Check(Order order) =>",
        "        order.Customer == _customer ? $\"customer {_customer} is blocked\" : null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "interface IEntity",
        "{",
        "    int Id { get; }",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Result<T>(bool IsOk, T? Value, string Error)",
        "{",
        "    public static Result<T> Ok(T value) => new(true, value, \"\");",
        "    public static Result<T> Fail(string error) => new(false, default, error);",
        "}",
        "",
        "interface IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    Result<T> Add(T item);",
        "    T? Find(int id);",
        "    IReadOnlyList<T> All();",
        "}",
        "",
        "class ListRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    private readonly List<T> _items = new();",
        "",
        "    public Result<T> Add(T item)",
        "    {",
        "        if (Find(item.Id) is not null)",
        "            return Result<T>.Fail($\"duplicate id {item.Id}\");",
        "        _items.Add(item);",
        "        return Result<T>.Ok(item);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public T? Find(int id) => _items.FirstOrDefault(i => i.Id == id);",
        "",
        "    public IReadOnlyList<T> All() => _items;",
        "}",
        "",
        "class SortedRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : IEntity",
        "{",
        "    private readonly SortedDictionary<int, T> _items = new();",
        "",
        "    public Result<T> Add(T item)",
        "    {",
        "        if (!_items.TryAdd(item.Id, item))",
        "            return Result<T>.Fail($\"duplicate id {item.Id}\");",
        "        return Result<T>.Ok(item);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public T? Find(int id) => _items.TryGetValue(id, out var item) ? item : default;",
        "",
        "    public IReadOnlyList<T> All() => _items.Values.ToList();",
        "}",
        "",
        "enum Status { Accepted, Rejected }",
        "",
        "record Outcome(Order Order, Status Status, string Reason);",
        "",
        "class OrderDesk",
        "{",
        "    private readonly List<IOrderRule> _rules;",
        "    private readonly IRepository<Order> _orders;",
        "",
        "    public OrderDesk(List<IOrderRule> rules, IRepository<Order> orders)",
        "    {",
        "        _rules = rules;",
        "        _orders = orders;",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public event Action<Outcome>? OrderProcessed;",
        "",
        "    public void Process(Order order)",
        "    {",
        "        var result = Validate(order);",
        "        if (result.IsOk)",
        "            result = _orders.Add(order);",
        "",
        "        var outcome = result.IsOk",
        "            ? new Outcome(order, Status.Accepted, \"\")",
        "            : new Outcome(order, Status.Rejected, result.Error);",
        "",
        "        OrderProcessed?.Invoke(outcome);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    private Result<Order> Validate(Order order)",
        "    {",
        "        var reasons = _rules.Select(rule => rule.Check(order)).OfType<string>().ToList();",
        "        return reasons.Count == 0",
        "            ? Result<Order>.Ok(order)",
        "            : Result<Order>.Fail(string.Join(\"; \", reasons));",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "class TotalsBoard",
        "{",
        "    private readonly Dictionary<Product, int> _units = new();",
        "",
        "    public int Accepted { get; private set; }",
        "    public int Rejected { get; private set; }",
        "",
        "    public void Record(Outcome outcome)",
        "    {",
        "        if (outcome.Status != Status.Accepted)",
        "        {",
        "            Rejected++;",
        "            return;",
        "        }",
        "",
        "        Accepted++;",
        "        _units[outcome.Order.Product] = _units.GetValueOrDefault(outcome.Order.Product) + outcome.Order.Quantity;",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public string UnitsLine() =>",
        "        _units.Count == 0",
        "            ? \"Units: none\"",
        "            : \"Units: \" + string.Join(\", \", _units.OrderBy(u => u.Key).Select(u => $\"{u.Key} {u.Value}\"));",
        "}"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "the board totals accepted units",
          "stdin": [
            "1,alice,widget,3",
            "2,bob,gadget,2",
            "3,carol,widget,4",
            "4,dave,gizmo,1",
            "5,erin,gadget,1"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
            "#2 bob Gadget x2 accepted",
            "#3 carol Widget x4 accepted",
            "#4 dave Gizmo x1 rejected: Gizmo is discontinued",
            "#5 erin Gadget x1 accepted",
            "Accepted: 4, Rejected: 1, Unreadable: 0",
            "Units: Widget 7, Gadget 3",
            "Stored: #1, #2, #3, #5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "duplicates and sorting still work",
          "stdin": [
            "7,bob,gadget,1",
            "1,alice,widget,3",
            "1,carol,widget,2",
            "3,dave,widget,2",
            "3,mallory,widget,1"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "#7 bob Gadget x1 accepted",
            "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
            "#1 carol Widget x2 rejected: duplicate id 1",
            "#3 dave Widget x2 accepted",
            "#3 mallory Widget x1 rejected: customer mallory is blocked",
            "Accepted: 3, Rejected: 2, Unreadable: 0",
            "Units: Widget 5, Gadget 1",
            "Stored: #1, #3, #7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "no input",
          "stdin": "",
          "expect": [
            "Accepted: 0, Rejected: 0, Unreadable: 0",
            "Units: none",
            "Stored: none"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "event\\s+Action<Outcome>\\??\\s+OrderProcessed",
          "message": "OrderDesk declares an OrderProcessed event"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "OrderProcessed\\s*\\?\\.\\s*Invoke",
          "message": "Raises the event with ?.Invoke"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "OrderProcessed\\s*\\+=\\s*board\\.Record",
          "message": "The board subscribes with board.Record"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "enum\\s+Status",
          "message": "Declares a Status enum"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`TotalsBoard` keeps a `Dictionary<Product, int>`; add with `_units[p] = _units.GetValueOrDefault(p) + quantity;`.",
        "`UnitsLine()`: `_units.OrderBy(u => u.Key)` sorts by the enum's order.",
        "The printing lambda: `desk.OrderProcessed += outcome => Console.WriteLine(Format(outcome));` with a `Format` helper that builds the same text as before."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "An audit log that can leave",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Add a third subscriber, and let it unsubscribe.",
        "",
        "1. Write `class AuditLog` with `IReadOnlyList<string> Entries` and `void Record(Outcome outcome)`, which adds `#ID status` with the status in lower case (`#2 rejected`).",
        "2. Subscribe `audit.Record` after the board.",
        "3. A line that is exactly `audit off` (spaces around it allowed) is a command, not an order: it unsubscribes the audit log with `-=` and is not counted as unreadable. Orders after it are still processed, printed and counted; they just are not audited.",
        "",
        "After the `Stored` line print `Audit: N entries` and then each entry indented by two spaces.",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "1,alice,widget,3",
        "2,bob,gadget,0",
        "audit off",
        "3,carol,widget,4",
        "bad line",
        "4,dave,gadget,2",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "#1 alice Widget x3 accepted",
        "#2 bob Gadget x0 rejected: quantity must be at least 1",
        "#3 carol Widget x4 accepted",
        "line 5: cannot read 'bad line'",
        "#4 dave Gadget x2 accepted",
        "Accepted: 3, Rejected: 1, Unreadable: 1",
        "Units: Widget 7, Gadget 2",
        "Stored: #1, #3, #4",
        "Audit: 2 entries",
        "  #1 accepted",
        "  #2 rejected",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var rules = new List<IOrderRule>",
        "{",
        "    new MinQuantityRule(),",
        "    new MaxQuantityRule(10),",
        "    new DiscontinuedRule(Product.Gizmo),",
        "    new BlockedCustomerRule(\"mallory\"),",
        "};",
        "",
        "IRepository<Order> orders = new SortedRepository<Order>();",
        "var desk = new OrderDesk(rules, orders);",
        "var board = new TotalsBoard();",
        "",
        "desk.OrderProcessed += outcome => Console.WriteLine(Format(outcome));",
        "desk.OrderProcessed += board.Record;",
